      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let the three numbers in the set be \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) where \\(a \\leq b \\leq c\\). Given that \\(a = 1\\), \\(b\\) (which is the median) could be 3, and \\(c\\) (the largest number) could be between 4 and 2 (since all numbers are integers and less than or equal to 4). Thus, our set would look something like \\([1, 3, c]\\). The median being 4 and the mean of the set being 4 implies that the sum of the numbers is 3s. Hence, we can write:\n\n\\[1 + 3 + c = 3s \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 4 + c = 3s\\] \n\nAlso,\n\\[\\frac{1 + 3 + c}{3} = 4 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{4 + c}{3} = 4 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 4 + c = 12 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad c = 8\\]\n\nTherefore, \\(c - a = 8 - 1 = \\boxed{7}\\).",
